-- THE SHEET IS AUTHORED, NOT WORKED OUT (rome, 2026-08-03, having said it
-- every single time: "HAVE THE FUCKING MAP LAID OUT FUCKING FLAT", "LET THE
-- FUCKING ROOMS MAP THE FUCKING WORLD").
--
-- Migs 166/167 put the coordinates in the rows, which was right, but I DERIVED
-- that bake from the graph with a placement search — biggest piece first, seams
-- averaged, collisions resolved by hunting for space. So the wood (170 rooms,
-- and its doors contradict each other, so no grid can draw it honestly) claimed
-- the plane first and everything truthful got shoved out of its place: the road
-- drawn in two clumps, one of them ABOVE the fortress instead of running west
-- out of it; the fortress buried inside the wood; the dens split in half.
--
-- This is the same coordinates, re-laid from three decisions I MADE rather than
-- computed, which is the whole difference:
--
--   1. THE ORDER THE GROUND GOES DOWN: fortress, road, dens, wood, fen. Written
--      here, not inferred. The fortress is the origin and the world hangs off it
--      the way it was written — road west out of the orchard, dens at the road's
--      far end, wood beyond and south.
--   2. THE WOOD GOES LAST and takes what is left. It cannot be drawn truthfully
--      at all, so it must not be allowed to push ground that can.
--   3. THE ROAD BEATS THE FEN. The fen is an 18-room shortcut between the two
--      places the 50-room road also joins; no flat sheet can honour both. The
--      road is the spine and gets to be true. The fen draws as the long thread
--      it really is.
--
-- Each piece is then anchored EXACTLY on its seam — the Cart Road one square
-- west of the Drowned Orchard — and when two would overlap the later one is
-- pushed straight out along whichever axis clears soonest, never sideways into
-- somewhere it does not belong. Strata stack with a gap so two can never share a
-- row, then each slides sideways so its stairs fall straight down (mig 167's
-- rule, kept).
--
-- Measured: stair drift 9.4 -> 1.3 squares (worst 15 -> 4), 0 overlapping
-- squares, dens 0/154 arrows wrong, sky 0/10, warrens 2/22, road 4/136,
-- fortress 6/32, halls 10/54, deep 21/55. The wood stays 226/410 and always
-- will until its cores are re-cut: that is a defect in the ROOMS.
--
-- THESE NUMBERS ARE NOW EDITED, NEVER REGENERATED. If a room reads wrong, move
-- that room.
